WEBVTT

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.595
Ah! The blood of my enemies
is forever immortalized

00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:31.857
on my &lt;i&gt;d'k tahg.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:37.341
I can still taste their
final panicked screams.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:41.562
My death will be ecstasy.

00:00:41.606 --> 00:00:44.130
A glorious end that will
take me straight to Sto'Vo'Kor.

00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:48.917
I have honored my house,
but will you?

00:00:48.961 --> 00:00:52.617
&lt;i&gt;How many soldiers
in the Klingon empire&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.053
&lt;i&gt;will be proving their&lt;/i&gt; toduj?

00:00:54.097 --> 00:00:56.838
- Four! &lt;i&gt;
- I heard... four.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:56.882 --> 00:01:00.929
&lt;i&gt;And so begins the greatest
adventure of your lives.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:03.802
&lt;i&gt;You will all die
on this quest,&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:03.845 --> 00:01:07.022
&lt;i&gt;but will you do it
with honor?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:10.678 --> 00:01:13.116
- Yeah!
- Honor!

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:25.623
Come on, natural 20.

00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:29.104
Qapla'! &lt;i&gt;
You've rolled an 18,&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.324
&lt;i&gt;which means the&lt;/i&gt; petaQ &lt;i&gt;
is frozen in fear&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:32.891
&lt;i&gt;by your battle cry.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.284
Okay, while he's cowering,

00:02:34.327 --> 00:02:36.547
I strike him down
with my &lt;i&gt;mek'leth.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.462
&lt;i&gt;- Your blow landed.&lt;/i&gt;
- Whoo!

00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:40.638
&lt;i&gt;But his brother swears revenge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:40.681 --> 00:02:42.640
&lt;i&gt;Reinforcements are on their way.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:42.683 --> 00:02:44.468
I can't believe Martok
recorded all this.

00:02:44.511 --> 00:02:46.339
You'd think he'd be too busy
being a chancellor and stuff.

00:02:46.383 --> 00:02:48.254
No, no, he didn't.
It's a Ferengi knockoff.

00:02:48.298 --> 00:02:50.256
They do it for all
the famous Klingons.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.736
I've been trying to get
the Gowron expansion for months.

00:02:51.779 --> 00:02:54.260
Ah, it's so nice to
all be back together.

00:02:54.304 --> 00:02:57.045
I needed a break from all
the battles and court-martials.

00:02:57.089 --> 00:02:58.743
It hasn't been a break for me.

00:02:58.786 --> 00:03:00.745
Ransom's made it his mission
to catch me messing up.

00:03:00.788 --> 00:03:02.181
He's been riding my ass

00:03:02.225 --> 00:03:03.791
just waiting for me
to break protocol.

00:03:03.835 --> 00:03:06.316
Ah, I would love to be
a number one's number one.

00:03:06.359 --> 00:03:08.274
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM [over comm]: Ensign
Mariner, where are you?&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:08.318 --> 00:03:10.015
In the repair bay,
repairing stuff.

00:03:10.058 --> 00:03:13.105
&lt;i&gt;When we have a mission briefing,
I expect you to be early.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:13.148 --> 00:03:14.280
It doesn't start for an hour!

00:03:14.324 --> 00:03:15.455
&lt;i&gt;I know. You're almost late&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:15.499 --> 00:03:16.978
&lt;i&gt;for being early. Move it!&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:17.022 --> 00:03:18.197
Are you coming, Rutherford?

00:03:18.241 --> 00:03:19.329
Nah, I want to finish playing.

00:03:19.372 --> 00:03:20.591
I'll just be regular early.

00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:25.987
I punch my own chest, excited
for more foes to vanquish.

00:03:26.031 --> 00:03:29.034
&lt;i&gt;Your battle chest punches fail
to boost your stamina.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:29.077 --> 00:03:30.688
- Dang it.
- You know, I think

00:03:30.731 --> 00:03:32.298
this whole Ransom thing
might be good for Mariner.

00:03:32.342 --> 00:03:33.778
She hasn't been in the brig
in forever.

00:03:33.821 --> 00:03:35.736
Yeah. Making the best
of a bad situation

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.303
worked for Vendome.

00:03:37.347 --> 00:03:39.218
That's how he got to
be captain so fast.

00:03:39.262 --> 00:03:41.525
Yeah, right.
Captain Vendome.

00:03:41.568 --> 00:03:42.700
Oh, can you imagine?

00:03:42.743 --> 00:03:43.962
What do you mean?
He's a captain.

00:03:44.005 --> 00:03:45.442
You didn't hear?

00:03:45.485 --> 00:03:47.792
Ha! Captain of what,
the USS &lt;i&gt;Gullible?&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:47.835 --> 00:03:49.097
Guys, I'm not falling for this.

00:03:49.141 --> 00:03:50.577
No, of the &lt;i&gt;Inglewood.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:50.621 --> 00:03:52.449
Yeah. He transferred there
months ago.

00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:54.015
Dude, are you messing
with us?

00:03:54.059 --> 00:03:56.061
The &lt;i&gt;Inglewood?&lt;/i&gt;
Tha-That's Chapman's ship.

00:03:56.104 --> 00:03:58.803
It was until a temporal rift
turned him into a baby.

00:03:58.846 --> 00:03:59.934
Vendome got a field promotion,

00:03:59.978 --> 00:04:01.762
- and it stuck.
- What?!

00:04:01.806 --> 00:04:04.330
But-but he's a goofball.

00:04:04.374 --> 00:04:05.418
Vendome's the guy who gets
hit with a spear

00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:06.941
on away missions.

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:08.421
Well, that goofball
breezed up the ranks.

00:04:08.465 --> 00:04:10.684
"...completing a meteoric rise
to captain."

00:04:10.728 --> 00:04:12.120
I can't believe this.

00:04:12.164 --> 00:04:13.861
Every single thing I do
is calculated

00:04:13.905 --> 00:04:15.472
to help me make captain one day,

00:04:15.515 --> 00:04:17.082
and this guy just lucks into it.

00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:18.779
I wouldn't say it was luck.

00:04:18.823 --> 00:04:21.434
Vendome was always saying yes
to new opportunities.

00:04:21.478 --> 00:04:23.915
He volunteered for any mission
he could, good or bad.

00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:25.960
- Now look at him.
- Tendi, it's not that easy.

00:04:26.004 --> 00:04:27.440
I can't just go
jumping into things

00:04:27.484 --> 00:04:28.876
without knowing the risks.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.225
&lt;i&gt;
Warrior, you discover&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.358
&lt;i&gt;a shortcut
through the caves of T'rachmor.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:32.402 --> 00:04:34.752
&lt;i&gt;Do you enter the darkness?&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:34.795 --> 00:04:36.841
No way. I'm not trying
to get cave killed.

00:04:36.884 --> 00:04:38.843
I'll stay on the path.

00:04:38.886 --> 00:04:41.976
&lt;i&gt;Ah! Ambush by House Dormat!&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.327
&lt;i&gt;You beg for your life
like a&lt;/i&gt; bIHnuch

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.981
and live out the rest
of your days not as a warrior

00:04:47.025 --> 00:04:48.548
but as a dentist.

00:04:48.592 --> 00:04:49.680
- Ouch.
- Aw, man.

00:04:49.723 --> 00:04:51.072
Brutal.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.208
&lt;i&gt;
Dulaine has a thermosphere&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:56.251 --> 00:04:57.644
&lt;i&gt;that's messy with charged ions,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:57.688 --> 00:04:59.429
&lt;i&gt;so transporters
are out of the picture.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:59.472 --> 00:05:01.561
&lt;i&gt;Instead, they've built
a system of orbital lifts,&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:01.605 --> 00:05:03.389
&lt;i&gt;one of which is malfunctioning.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:05.348
So, it's
a broken-down space elevator?

00:05:05.391 --> 00:05:06.697
They're not elevators.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.786
- They're orbital lifts.

00:05:12.964 --> 00:05:14.357
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is hosting

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.228
all the passengers
who got stuck here

00:05:16.271 --> 00:05:18.970
while we repair and coordinate
with Dulainians on the ground.

00:05:19.013 --> 00:05:21.538
All right. Ooh,
coordinating is my specialty.

00:05:21.581 --> 00:05:23.061
These guys
are one of those sexy cultures

00:05:23.104 --> 00:05:24.541
that run everywhere
and kiss hello, right?

00:05:24.584 --> 00:05:27.326
Their society
is wellness-based, yes.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:30.285
Well-yes, let's get down there
and get the party started.

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:32.070
&lt;i&gt;We&lt;/i&gt; aren't going anywhere.

00:05:32.113 --> 00:05:34.942
Mr. Billups, you and your man
are heading planetside

00:05:34.986 --> 00:05:37.597
- to liaise with the Dulainians.
- What?!

00:05:37.641 --> 00:05:39.120
Really? I mean,

00:05:39.164 --> 00:05:41.035
usually engineers
are the ones who do the repairs,

00:05:41.079 --> 00:05:42.646
but if that's what you want, then...

00:05:42.689 --> 00:05:44.387
But they'd be better
and faster at this than us.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.171
Don't question my orders, Ensign.

00:05:46.214 --> 00:05:48.260
We're perfectly capable
of repairing an elev...

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:49.957
uh, an orbital lift.

00:05:50.001 --> 00:05:52.482
Mr. Billups, just give
the Dulainians our greetings,

00:05:52.525 --> 00:05:54.919
keep them apprised
of the repairs and, uh...

00:05:54.962 --> 00:05:57.617
Try not to have
too much fun down there.

00:05:57.661 --> 00:05:59.663
- Yes, sir.

00:06:06.713 --> 00:06:08.585
Hmm.

00:06:10.151 --> 00:06:11.631
Did you know that Vendome

00:06:11.675 --> 00:06:13.111
staffed his whole bridge crew
with Bolians?

00:06:13.154 --> 00:06:15.243
Ooh, I didn't.
But that's really cool.

00:06:15.287 --> 00:06:17.158
I know, right?

00:06:17.202 --> 00:06:19.639
No matter how careful I am,
no matter how hard I try,

00:06:19.683 --> 00:06:21.206
I feel like I'm gonna be
an ensign

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:22.642
- for the rest of my life.
- Again,

00:06:22.686 --> 00:06:24.470
if planning and trying
aren't working,

00:06:24.514 --> 00:06:26.167
maybe don't do that.

00:06:26.211 --> 00:06:28.169
- You sound like Mariner.
- Well, look at me.

00:06:28.213 --> 00:06:30.955
It wasn't my plan to get into
senior science officer training.

00:06:30.998 --> 00:06:32.696
It just happened.
And now I've got

00:06:32.739 --> 00:06:34.959
so much new stuff to study,
and I'm loving it!

00:06:35.002 --> 00:06:37.222
That could be you
if you tried something new.

00:06:37.265 --> 00:06:38.876
Yo, Boimler.

00:06:38.919 --> 00:06:40.617
We got an open spot
in the springball tournament.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.619
We need a wiry dude
who's hard to hit.

00:06:42.662 --> 00:06:44.316
- You want in?
- Sweaty muscleheads

00:06:44.359 --> 00:06:46.927
drilling balls at my face?
No, thanks.

00:06:46.971 --> 00:06:49.713
Wow. Could've just said no, man.

00:06:49.756 --> 00:06:51.845
Boimler. Vendome?

00:06:52.846 --> 00:06:54.108
Uh, wait!

00:06:54.152 --> 00:06:55.370
Sherwyns, I'm in.

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.981
Let's-let's do this. Let's, uh,

00:06:57.024 --> 00:06:59.157
spring that ball.

00:07:07.644 --> 00:07:09.907
Good game, Ensign.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.125
- I'm impressed.

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:12.866
By my athletic ab-b-bility?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.608
What? No, no, no.
By that sustained scream

00:07:15.652 --> 00:07:18.742
when I bowled you over.
You were really wailing.

00:07:18.785 --> 00:07:21.005
Thanks. I get a lot of practice.

00:07:21.048 --> 00:07:23.660
Listen, I run a choir
when I'm off duty.

00:07:23.703 --> 00:07:26.401
Bajoran dirges.
I've been looking for a soprano.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:27.664
You interested?

00:07:27.707 --> 00:07:29.579
A dirge choir? I...

00:07:29.622 --> 00:07:31.972
will try that. Sure, yeah.

00:07:32.016 --> 00:07:34.409
- Let's, uh, let's get dirgey.
- All right!

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.586
That's the ticket.
You're gonna have a blast!

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:40.111
We've got the saddest dirges
in the quadrant.

00:07:47.422 --> 00:07:49.555
You honor the Prophets

00:07:49.599 --> 00:07:51.078
with that pitch, Bradward.

00:07:51.122 --> 00:07:54.952
If you ever need a favor,
I'm a combadge tap away.

00:07:54.995 --> 00:07:58.042
Really? Uh, wow.
Uh, thank you, sir.

00:07:58.085 --> 00:07:59.478
Mr. Boimler.

00:07:59.522 --> 00:08:01.349
Aah! Geez, Lundy, you're too...

00:08:01.393 --> 00:08:02.742
Oh, you're too scary, man.

00:08:02.786 --> 00:08:03.743
You can't jump out
at people like that.

00:08:03.787 --> 00:08:05.179
Can I guess your weight?

00:08:05.223 --> 00:08:08.443
I'd peg you
at a healthy 61.2 kilos.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:11.621
Wow. Uh, yeah.
That's e-exactly right.

00:08:11.664 --> 00:08:15.407
Mm. My figure drawing class
needs a skeletal boy

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:17.757
for our life drawing
this afternoon.

00:08:17.801 --> 00:08:19.716
Have you ever sat for oil?

00:08:19.759 --> 00:08:22.066
Uh...

00:08:22.109 --> 00:08:24.068
Oil me up.

00:08:27.114 --> 00:08:28.942
Ow.

00:08:28.986 --> 00:08:31.858
- What the hell even is this?
- [grunting] 20.

00:08:31.902 --> 00:08:33.817
I hope you're-- 21--

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.470
being careful not to-- 22--

00:08:35.514 --> 00:08:37.211
misalign the dampeners. 23.

00:08:37.255 --> 00:08:39.126
Are you really lifting
right now?

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:41.955
I'd barely call this
lifting. Oh, yeah.

00:08:41.999 --> 00:08:43.304
You know,
two people working on this

00:08:43.348 --> 00:08:45.132
would get it done
so much faster.

00:08:45.176 --> 00:08:47.482
You know,
like two engineer-type people?

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:50.485
Can an engineer do that?

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:52.357
Uh, yeah. With a step stool.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.489
&lt;i&gt;Billups
to Commander Ransom. Come in.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.622
How's it going
down there, Billups?

00:08:56.666 --> 00:08:59.233
I'll tell you, these Dulainians
are a friendly people.

00:08:59.277 --> 00:09:01.627
You know they kiss
instead of shaking hands?

00:09:01.671 --> 00:09:04.282
&lt;i&gt;- With tongue!
- Yeah, with tongue.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:04.325 --> 00:09:06.589
Control yourself,
Andy. We wouldn't want you

00:09:06.632 --> 00:09:08.634
to accidentally become a king
down there.

00:09:08.678 --> 00:09:09.983
I don't know if I'll have time.

00:09:10.027 --> 00:09:11.376
Because we have a dance
coming up,

00:09:11.419 --> 00:09:13.813
then a feast
and then a drinking competition.

00:09:13.857 --> 00:09:15.293
Are you for real?

00:09:15.336 --> 00:09:16.903
&lt;i&gt;I could get real
used to this kind of treatment.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:16.947 --> 00:09:19.384
&lt;i&gt;Maybe I should transfer
divisions again.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:20.777 --> 00:09:22.387
We'll join you guys
when we're done up here.

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:24.476
- The repairs seem simple enough.

00:09:24.519 --> 00:09:27.479
&lt;i&gt;Mmm. Did you remember
to decouple the flow inverters&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:27.522 --> 00:09:29.481
&lt;i&gt;before reconnecting
the conduit piping?&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:29.524 --> 00:09:31.744
Uh...
Of course I did. Who wouldn't?

00:09:31.788 --> 00:09:33.267
&lt;i&gt;
Great. Well, I got to go.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:33.311 --> 00:09:35.052
&lt;i&gt;There's some sort
of wrestling display on,&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:35.095 --> 00:09:36.662
&lt;i&gt;and they need a judge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:36.706 --> 00:09:38.185
&lt;i&gt;
Oh, yeah, baby! Let's go!&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:38.229 --> 00:09:39.839
&lt;i&gt;Did&lt;/i&gt; you decouple
the flow inverters?

00:09:39.883 --> 00:09:42.407
Of course I did.
Just focus on your own work.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.843
You know, it's not a big deal

00:09:43.887 --> 00:09:45.584
to admit
that we should be down there

00:09:45.628 --> 00:09:47.064
and they should be up here.

00:09:47.107 --> 00:09:48.805
Starfleet
isn't all about being fed fruit

00:09:48.848 --> 00:09:51.242
by erotic aliens with
slightly different nose ridges.

00:09:51.285 --> 00:09:53.374
Sometimes
you got to get your hands dirty.

00:09:53.418 --> 00:09:56.160
Engineers would've been done
with this hours ago.

00:09:56.203 --> 00:09:57.814
Arguing
with your commanding officer

00:09:57.857 --> 00:10:00.381
isn't gonna get the job done
any sooner.

00:10:00.425 --> 00:10:02.209
Aah! Oh, no. Oh, no,

00:10:02.253 --> 00:10:04.081
- no, no, no, no.

00:10:11.523 --> 00:10:13.438
- Oh, hey.

00:10:13.481 --> 00:10:15.135
Hey.
What's with all the new faces?

00:10:15.179 --> 00:10:16.702
We're hosting
everyone that got stranded

00:10:16.746 --> 00:10:18.443
on the orbital lift
while it gets repaired.

00:10:18.486 --> 00:10:20.837
That's cool. Listen,
you were totally right earlier.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.577
I've been saying yes
to everything today,

00:10:22.621 --> 00:10:24.144
going way outside
my comfort zone,

00:10:24.188 --> 00:10:26.059
and so far,
Shaxs says he owes me a favor,

00:10:26.103 --> 00:10:27.844
I'm not afraid
of Chief Lundy anymore...

00:10:27.887 --> 00:10:30.498
It's just been
a really great day.

00:10:30.542 --> 00:10:32.196
Oh, I love that for you, Boims.

00:10:32.239 --> 00:10:33.806
See?
When you get rid of the plan,

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:35.373
you leave room for good things.

00:10:35.416 --> 00:10:38.724
From now on, the new plan
is say yes to everything.

00:10:38.768 --> 00:10:40.160
But that's, uh, still a plan.

00:10:40.204 --> 00:10:41.727
How about just no plan?

00:10:41.771 --> 00:10:43.860
Nope. Today, I am a new Boimler.

00:10:43.903 --> 00:10:45.688
A bold Boimler.

00:10:45.731 --> 00:10:47.777
And the next person
who asks me to do something,

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.083
I'm saying yes no matter what.

00:10:50.127 --> 00:10:52.085
- K'RANCH: Excuse me.

00:10:52.129 --> 00:10:53.783
I am K'Ranch.

00:10:53.826 --> 00:10:56.742
I was supposed to be
on the planet by now,

00:10:56.786 --> 00:10:58.918
but the space elevator
is broken.

00:10:58.962 --> 00:11:01.007
Hi, K'Ranch.
Welcome to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:01.051 --> 00:11:03.836
I'm Tendi, and this is Boimler.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:07.971
K'RANCH: My species has an
undeniable natural urge to hunt.

00:11:08.014 --> 00:11:11.888
This delay to the planet
has been weighing on me.

00:11:11.931 --> 00:11:14.804
Would either of you
be willing to...

00:11:16.762 --> 00:11:19.243
...be willing to be hunted?

00:11:19.286 --> 00:11:21.636
Oh, no, thank you.
Maybe you should see

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.290
if Dr. T'Ana can help you out
in sickbay.

00:11:23.334 --> 00:11:24.857
Wait. Uh, Mr. K'Ranch,

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:26.685
I'm gonna say yes to the hunted.

00:11:26.729 --> 00:11:28.687
- To-to being hunted.
- Uh...

00:11:28.731 --> 00:11:30.820
Uh, just because you said
you were going to say yes

00:11:30.863 --> 00:11:32.473
to the next person
who asked you to do something

00:11:32.517 --> 00:11:33.823
doesn't mean
you have to do &lt;i&gt;this.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:33.866 --> 00:11:35.389
You can do the next one.

00:11:35.433 --> 00:11:36.826
Eh, you're right...

00:11:36.869 --> 00:11:38.871
is what the old Boimler
would have said.

00:11:38.915 --> 00:11:40.873
It would be an honor
if you hunted me, sir.

00:11:40.917 --> 00:11:42.527
Let's do it.

00:11:48.925 --> 00:11:53.538
You are now my prey.

00:11:53.581 --> 00:11:57.368
The hunt begins in one hour.

00:12:02.068 --> 00:12:03.809
It won't be as bad as it sounds.

00:12:03.853 --> 00:12:05.637
What are you doing?!
You only have an hour!

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:08.509
- Run! Run! Run!

00:12:14.864 --> 00:12:16.561
&lt;i&gt;At this point,
everything should be lining up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:16.604 --> 00:12:19.172
&lt;i&gt;All you need to do is align
the magnetic seal on the panel,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:19.216 --> 00:12:21.218
&lt;i&gt;and the repair is complete.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:21.261 --> 00:12:22.610
Magnetic seal? I don't even...

00:12:22.654 --> 00:12:23.786
What the hell
is she talking about?

00:12:25.744 --> 00:12:27.485
Billups,
these space elevators use

00:12:27.528 --> 00:12:28.703
Federation standard
measurements, right?

00:12:28.747 --> 00:12:30.705
&lt;i&gt;Uh, we've run into a little bit&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:30.749 --> 00:12:32.272
&lt;i&gt;of a diplomacy problem
down here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:32.316 --> 00:12:33.926
You dare enter the sacred hall

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:35.449
&lt;i&gt;without an exposed navel?!&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:35.493 --> 00:12:37.843
&lt;i&gt;Oh! I'm sorry. I didn't know.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:37.887 --> 00:12:39.671
What's going on down there?
It sounds a little tense.

00:12:39.714 --> 00:12:41.934
&lt;i&gt;Uh, well, I don't know how well
you know Dulainian religion,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:41.978 --> 00:12:43.980
&lt;i&gt;but we weren't wearing the right
outfits in the right place,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:44.023 --> 00:12:45.895
&lt;i&gt;and now the locals are getting
pretty testy, so maybe,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:45.938 --> 00:12:47.853
&lt;i&gt;sir, you could, uh, come down
here and help smooth things out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:47.897 --> 00:12:49.289
&lt;i&gt;- That would be great.&lt;/i&gt;
- Ha!

00:12:49.333 --> 00:12:50.682
I knew it. All right, let's go.

00:12:50.725 --> 00:12:52.031
No can do, Billups.

00:12:52.075 --> 00:12:53.163
What?

00:12:53.206 --> 00:12:54.773
We still have work to do
up here.

00:12:54.817 --> 00:12:56.644
Show them your belly buttons.
You'll be fine.

00:12:56.688 --> 00:12:58.603
&lt;i&gt;We tried that,
and it just made them angrier.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:58.646 --> 00:13:01.040
&lt;i&gt;No, look. Our B-buttons
are out and about.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:01.084 --> 00:13:02.868
Just explain
that we respect all cultures

00:13:02.912 --> 00:13:04.739
and, you know, morality

00:13:04.783 --> 00:13:06.741
and the Prime Directive
and all that stuff.

00:13:06.785 --> 00:13:09.396
&lt;i&gt;Okay, I'll try it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.225
Jack... Uh, sir, okay,
you've made your point.

00:13:12.269 --> 00:13:14.967
Can we please just go down there
and lend a diplomatic hand?

00:13:15.011 --> 00:13:17.056
Billups can rebuild the
navigation computer blindfolded.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.102
I think he can handle
some angry locals.

00:13:19.145 --> 00:13:20.973
He clearly can't!
Is it really worth

00:13:21.017 --> 00:13:23.193
endangering those guys
just to get under my skin?

00:13:23.236 --> 00:13:24.542
My command decisions

00:13:24.585 --> 00:13:26.500
have nothing to do
with your sensitivities.

00:13:26.544 --> 00:13:28.981
You need to learn how to trust
your superiors, Ensign.

00:13:29.025 --> 00:13:31.244
Fine.
I'm gonna go work over there

00:13:31.288 --> 00:13:32.767
so I don't have to watch you
fumble around

00:13:32.811 --> 00:13:34.334
- with that stupid pipe.
- I'm not fumbling!

00:13:42.386 --> 00:13:45.215
Uh, hello? Mr. K'Ranch, sir?

00:13:45.258 --> 00:13:47.913
What do you want, prey?

00:13:47.957 --> 00:13:49.393
I was just wondering,
when you say

00:13:49.436 --> 00:13:51.221
you're gonna hunt me,
you mean, like,

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:53.571
- metaphorically, right?

00:13:55.312 --> 00:13:57.749
K'RANCH: There are only
three types of prey.

00:13:57.792 --> 00:13:59.490
You are the first type:

00:13:59.533 --> 00:14:01.927
immobilized by your fear.

00:14:01.971 --> 00:14:04.930
The second type
scurries away to hide,

00:14:04.974 --> 00:14:07.890
delaying the inevitable.

00:14:07.933 --> 00:14:09.326
Uh, what's the third kind?

00:14:09.369 --> 00:14:11.545
The third
is a winged lizard-type creature

00:14:11.589 --> 00:14:13.156
that doesn't really apply
to you.

00:14:13.199 --> 00:14:15.158
Oh, okay. Yeah. No,
I'm just gonna scurry away

00:14:15.201 --> 00:14:17.682
while I think about it.
When does the hunt start?

00:14:17.725 --> 00:14:20.119
It already has!

00:14:42.446 --> 00:14:44.796
Oh, no!

00:14:46.276 --> 00:14:48.147
No, no, no!

00:14:56.025 --> 00:14:57.591
Someone's trying to kill me!

00:15:07.775 --> 00:15:09.734
Captain, you got to help me.
I'm being hunted.

00:15:09.777 --> 00:15:11.605
What? Not on my ship.

00:15:11.649 --> 00:15:13.129
That's totally unacceptable.

00:15:13.172 --> 00:15:15.696
Security,
I need a team on Deck Three.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:18.308
Oh, thank God. It's this big guy
called K'Ranch.

00:15:18.351 --> 00:15:19.874
I told him he could hunt me
in the bar,

00:15:19.918 --> 00:15:21.485
- but that was a mistake, and...
- K'Ranch?

00:15:21.528 --> 00:15:23.095
Well, that's different.

00:15:23.139 --> 00:15:25.489
- Security, belay that order.
- What?!

00:15:25.532 --> 00:15:28.666
I shared a lovely brunch
earlier today with K'Ranch.

00:15:28.709 --> 00:15:30.885
: You know,
he's quite the charmer.

00:15:30.929 --> 00:15:33.453
I'm glad he found someone
to partake in his Venarix hunt.

00:15:33.497 --> 00:15:35.455
But I don't want to be hit
with an arrow or a boomerang

00:15:35.499 --> 00:15:37.022
or any of that. Please, Captain.

00:15:37.066 --> 00:15:39.285
Ensign,
we have to respect his culture.

00:15:39.329 --> 00:15:41.113
And didn't you give him
your word?

00:15:41.157 --> 00:15:42.985
- I want my word back.

00:15:43.028 --> 00:15:45.596
- Oh, he's good. You better run.

00:15:45.639 --> 00:15:48.860
- Thanks again for the mimosas.
- My pleasure.

00:15:48.903 --> 00:15:50.731
- Happy hunting.

00:15:52.559 --> 00:15:54.344
&lt;i&gt;Sir, we could
really use your help.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:54.387 --> 00:15:56.520
&lt;i&gt;The Dulainians saw that
Lieutenant Billups had an outie,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:56.563 --> 00:15:58.217
&lt;i&gt;and now he's being sacrificed
to Morgo,&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:58.261 --> 00:16:00.437
&lt;i&gt;which I think
is a sentient volcano.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.047
&lt;i&gt;Help!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:02.091 --> 00:16:04.441
Just demand to parley
with their leader

00:16:04.484 --> 00:16:07.226
and explain they cannot
sacrifice Mr. Billups. Okay?

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:09.533
Straight spine.
Speak from the diaphragm.

00:16:09.576 --> 00:16:11.361
&lt;i&gt;Right. Okay. Also, their leader&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:11.404 --> 00:16:13.319
&lt;i&gt;is either an ancient god
or a telepathic baby.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:13.363 --> 00:16:14.842
&lt;i&gt;They're kind of dancing
around it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:14.886 --> 00:16:17.497
Sounds like you're
narrowing it down. You got this.

00:16:17.541 --> 00:16:18.846
&lt;i&gt;
Uh, right. Okay.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.196
&lt;i&gt;I'll speak from the diaphragm.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:20.239 --> 00:16:21.719
&lt;i&gt;
Help me!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:21.762 --> 00:16:23.199
&lt;i&gt;- I demand parley!
- Help!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:23.242 --> 00:16:24.722
&lt;i&gt;- Hello? Someone?&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:26.941 --> 00:16:29.031
Oh!

00:16:29.074 --> 00:16:30.771
Ugh! I'm gonna do it.

00:16:30.815 --> 00:16:31.946
I'm just gonna do it.
I don't care.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:33.035
I don't care. All right.

00:16:39.519 --> 00:16:40.912
I'm coming, Ruthy!

00:16:50.922 --> 00:16:51.879
Yeah!

00:16:55.361 --> 00:16:56.928
&lt;i&gt;
Ransom to Mariner. Come in.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:56.971 --> 00:16:58.321
Crap.

00:16:58.364 --> 00:16:59.844
What's up, sir?

00:16:59.887 --> 00:17:02.368
Mariner, I was, uh...
What's that sound?

00:17:02.412 --> 00:17:04.109
&lt;i&gt;- Is that wind?&lt;/i&gt;
- Uh, I, uh...

00:17:04.153 --> 00:17:07.547
I had to open up an exterior
pressure conduit. Oh!

00:17:07.591 --> 00:17:09.332
Ah, right.
The old pressure conduit.

00:17:09.375 --> 00:17:11.856
Well, I've been doing some
thinking, and you were right.

00:17:11.899 --> 00:17:13.858
I was going out of my way
to try to prove

00:17:13.901 --> 00:17:16.817
that you would disobey my orders
if you felt you knew better.

00:17:16.861 --> 00:17:19.951
&lt;i&gt;But you stayed on task.
You didn't go rogue.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:19.994 --> 00:17:21.822
Oh, uh, yeah. Yeah.

00:17:21.866 --> 00:17:24.434
&lt;i&gt;Anyway, listen, those engineers
are in way over their heads.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:24.477 --> 00:17:26.349
&lt;i&gt;It's time for us
to go save their butts.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:26.392 --> 00:17:28.351
&lt;i&gt;I'll come meet you
in Section Eight.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:31.093 --> 00:17:32.485
-  &lt;i&gt;
- What? You okay?&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:32.529 --> 00:17:35.009
I-I-I was just saying, "Yah!

00:17:35.053 --> 00:17:37.099
Sounds good," sir.

00:17:56.988 --> 00:18:00.034
Where are you, prey?

00:18:02.298 --> 00:18:06.128
&lt;i&gt;...am a proud soldier
of the Klingon Empire!&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:06.171 --> 00:18:07.172
- Shut it.

00:18:07.216 --> 00:18:09.131
Shut up. Shut up. Shut up.

00:18:09.174 --> 00:18:10.958
Stupid Ferengi program.

00:18:11.002 --> 00:18:13.396
&lt;i&gt;Warrior,
fight to the last breath.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:13.439 --> 00:18:15.615
Easy for you to say.
I'm not a Klingon.

00:18:15.659 --> 00:18:19.097
I-I-I tried to be bold today,
but I just ended up as prey.

00:18:19.141 --> 00:18:21.186
&lt;i&gt;The only way you can lose now
is by letting&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:23.275
&lt;i&gt;your foe define who you are.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:23.319 --> 00:18:25.973
&lt;i&gt;Never back down! Never cower!&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:35.026 --> 00:18:37.898
The hunt is on.

00:18:37.942 --> 00:18:40.118
- K'Ranch!

00:18:41.163 --> 00:18:42.425
I am not your prey.

00:18:42.468 --> 00:18:44.905
I am Bold Boimler!

00:18:44.949 --> 00:18:46.733
I haven't backed down all day,

00:18:46.777 --> 00:18:48.605
and I'm not starting now.

00:18:48.648 --> 00:18:51.912
You better run,
because now the hunted

00:18:51.956 --> 00:18:53.262
has become...

00:18:53.305 --> 00:18:54.741
Oh, my God!

00:18:54.785 --> 00:18:56.613
- No, no, no!

00:18:56.656 --> 00:19:00.921
The hunted always tries
to become the hunter.

00:19:00.965 --> 00:19:03.315
Tale old as time.

00:19:03.359 --> 00:19:05.796
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!
I didn't say you could kill me.

00:19:05.839 --> 00:19:08.059
Stop! Please!

00:19:10.409 --> 00:19:12.324
And with that,
my hunt has ended.

00:19:12.368 --> 00:19:14.239
Y-You're not gonna kill me?

00:19:14.283 --> 00:19:16.763
Kromsapiods
practice catch and release.

00:19:16.807 --> 00:19:18.983
We respect life above all else.

00:19:19.026 --> 00:19:20.289
That's why we hunt.

00:19:20.332 --> 00:19:21.507
Oh, thank God.

00:19:21.551 --> 00:19:23.074
You were excellent prey,

00:19:23.117 --> 00:19:24.554
but I do have notes.

00:19:24.597 --> 00:19:26.904
Can you maybe give them to me
in sickbay?

00:19:26.947 --> 00:19:29.298
When you decide to switch it up
and become the hunter,

00:19:29.341 --> 00:19:31.604
you can't just announce it
and stand there.

00:19:31.648 --> 00:19:33.171
Stick and move, you know?

00:19:33.215 --> 00:19:34.999
Uh-huh, yeah.
I'll keep that in mind.

00:19:35.042 --> 00:19:37.697
You have earned my respect,
Bradward Boimler.

00:19:37.741 --> 00:19:40.918
I will be passing along
high praise to your captain.

00:19:40.961 --> 00:19:43.921
Really? Thank you.

00:19:43.964 --> 00:19:48.230
Maybe just one more
for the boys back home.

00:19:53.235 --> 00:19:55.280
Climbing wall? For real?

00:19:55.324 --> 00:19:56.803
This stupid society

00:19:56.847 --> 00:20:00.198
built on exercise and wellness.

00:20:00.242 --> 00:20:02.331
Okay.

00:20:05.725 --> 00:20:08.250
Whoa!

00:20:14.604 --> 00:20:16.388
Sorry I'm late.
Had to make a quick trip

00:20:16.432 --> 00:20:18.303
- to the little commanders' room.
- No biggie.

00:20:18.347 --> 00:20:20.305
I've just been waiting here
the whole time.

00:20:20.349 --> 00:20:22.002
This is gonna sound crazy, Mariner,

00:20:22.046 --> 00:20:23.439
but since we don't have
a shuttle

00:20:23.482 --> 00:20:25.179
and the elevator
still won't descend,

00:20:25.223 --> 00:20:27.443
we're gonna have
to skydive down.

00:20:27.486 --> 00:20:30.141
Oh, wow. That's a wild plan,
sir. It's wild.

00:20:30.184 --> 00:20:32.622
I know. But if we hurry,
we can make it in time.

00:20:32.665 --> 00:20:34.493
Maybe...
Maybe we take a quick break?

00:20:34.537 --> 00:20:36.190
Good one.

00:20:36.234 --> 00:20:38.018
- Let's roll.

00:20:38.062 --> 00:20:40.847
Yeah!

00:20:52.946 --> 00:20:56.472
We come to you,
Volcanic Lord Morgo!

00:20:56.515 --> 00:20:58.212
Navel of the Planet!

00:20:58.256 --> 00:21:01.041
We sacrifice these sinners
in the name

00:21:01.085 --> 00:21:03.348
of Mendrick,
our psychic baby leader,

00:21:03.392 --> 00:21:06.351
and his coleader, 355,

00:21:06.395 --> 00:21:08.745
the sentient computer!

00:21:08.788 --> 00:21:11.443
Ooh, they weren't lying.
This did get complicated.

00:21:11.487 --> 00:21:14.925
Wow. Psychic baby,
evil computer &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; a volcano?

00:21:14.968 --> 00:21:16.230
You guys ever heard of overkill?

00:21:16.274 --> 00:21:18.189
It provides a system

00:21:18.232 --> 00:21:21.061
of checks and balances.

00:21:21.105 --> 00:21:23.194
&lt;i&gt;How dare you question
our method of governance.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:23.237 --> 00:21:24.587
&lt;i&gt;Throw them in the volcano.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:29.983 --> 00:21:31.202
For what it's worth, sir,

00:21:31.245 --> 00:21:33.073
it was an honor
serving with you.

00:21:33.117 --> 00:21:35.598
Oh, Samanthan,
the honor is mine.

00:21:35.641 --> 00:21:37.339
Wait!

00:21:37.382 --> 00:21:39.384
I demand parley!

00:21:39.428 --> 00:21:41.995
You live a health-based way
of life, correct?

00:21:42.039 --> 00:21:43.736
Yes.

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:45.651
It is our highest calling.

00:21:46.783 --> 00:21:49.046
- Then behold.

00:21:50.787 --> 00:21:52.179
Wow.

00:21:52.223 --> 00:21:55.357
Your lava tubes are perfect.

00:21:55.400 --> 00:21:57.402
&lt;i&gt;
You are wise, Starfleet.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:57.446 --> 00:21:58.490
&lt;i&gt;We will hear you out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:58.534 --> 00:22:00.405
Although we all come

00:22:00.449 --> 00:22:04.061
from different worlds,
we are only slightly different.

00:22:07.281 --> 00:22:09.719
- Yo, yo.

00:22:09.762 --> 00:22:11.808
You, uh,
you wanted to see me, sir?

00:22:11.851 --> 00:22:13.549
I owe you an apology. I assumed

00:22:13.592 --> 00:22:15.899
you'd be looking
for ways to piss me off

00:22:15.942 --> 00:22:18.118
and flame out.
I was wrong to push it.

00:22:18.162 --> 00:22:21.600
Thanks. I-I really want to stay
on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:21.644 --> 00:22:24.603
I-It was good work today,
but this was just one day.

00:22:24.647 --> 00:22:26.344
Don't think it erased
all the insubordination

00:22:26.388 --> 00:22:28.041
I've gotten from you
in the past.

00:22:28.085 --> 00:22:30.043
Yep. Yes, sir. Message received.

00:22:31.088 --> 00:22:34.396
Sir, you were really impressive
down there,

00:22:34.439 --> 00:22:36.093
the way you navigated
that volcano

00:22:36.136 --> 00:22:37.486
and the baby and all that.

00:22:37.529 --> 00:22:38.661
Save it for your personal log, Mariner.

00:22:38.704 --> 00:22:40.053
Buttering me up
is not gonna make

00:22:40.097 --> 00:22:41.533
your life any easier.

00:22:41.577 --> 00:22:42.795
All right.

00:22:44.406 --> 00:22:47.278
Yeah, I was pretty impressive.

00:22:47.321 --> 00:22:49.672
So, Ransom's a dick,
and I hate him.

00:22:49.715 --> 00:22:51.413
Oh, sounds like today went well.

00:22:51.456 --> 00:22:53.458
I mean, he did keep me
from getting dumped into lava.

00:22:53.502 --> 00:22:55.982
No. He was the whole reason
you were dangling over the lava

00:22:56.026 --> 00:22:57.897
- to start with.
- Nah. That was on me.

00:22:57.941 --> 00:22:59.508
I really should have had
my belly button out.

00:23:00.683 --> 00:23:02.815
&lt;i&gt;You eat breakfast
and gain plus-three stamina!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:02.859 --> 00:23:04.426
Damn,
they really programmed Martok

00:23:04.469 --> 00:23:06.602
with, like, full intensity
at all times.

00:23:06.645 --> 00:23:09.343
Hey, there he is.
How's the shoulder?

00:23:09.387 --> 00:23:12.172
Dr. T'Ana says it'll probably
always feel a little off,

00:23:12.216 --> 00:23:13.739
- but it's fine.
- Uh, sorry.

00:23:13.783 --> 00:23:15.524
I kind of feel responsible
since I was the one

00:23:15.567 --> 00:23:16.960
who told you
to go against your plans.

00:23:17.003 --> 00:23:18.657
All those years
of trying too hard

00:23:18.701 --> 00:23:20.529
never got me half the
recognition that I got today.

00:23:20.572 --> 00:23:21.965
Plus nerve damage.

00:23:22.008 --> 00:23:23.880
Plans are officially
out the air lock.

00:23:23.923 --> 00:23:26.273
I'm Bold Boimler
from here on out.

00:23:26.317 --> 00:23:28.885
I'm not sure that was the lesson
to learn today, you know?

00:23:28.928 --> 00:23:30.713
Uh, how about moderation?

00:23:30.756 --> 00:23:32.279
Old Boimler was into moderation.

00:23:32.323 --> 00:23:34.151
Bold Boimler is into boldness.

00:23:34.194 --> 00:23:37.763
I confidently enter the bar
and demand bloodwine.

00:23:37.807 --> 00:23:41.114
&lt;i&gt;The bartender rips your arm off
and kills you with it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:41.158 --> 00:23:42.638
&lt;i&gt;It is not an honorable death&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:42.681 --> 00:23:45.554
&lt;i&gt;since, technically,
you have died by your own hand.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:45.597 --> 00:23:47.381
Ah, whatever.
I'm still gonna be bold.

00:23:47.425 --> 00:23:49.166
&lt;i&gt;
If you'd like to continue,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:49.209 --> 00:23:51.734
&lt;i&gt;download the expansion pack,&lt;/i&gt;
Dinner with Lady Lindor.

00:23:51.777 --> 00:23:54.127
- Aw, come on! &lt;i&gt;
- You can subscribe&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:54.171 --> 00:23:56.478
&lt;i&gt;to the entire honorable season
by tapping here,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:56.521 --> 00:23:59.568
&lt;i&gt;or purchase your worthy
adventures à la carte.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:59.611 --> 00:24:02.614
&lt;i&gt;Ferengi black market tax
not included. All sales final.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:02.631 --> 00:25:06.631
Chirp.
